.TH SHOAL-TOKEN 1 "July 2026" "Shoal 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
shoal-token \- manage Shoal capability tokens
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B shoal-token create
.I principal
.RI [ profile ]
.RI [ \-\-cap " cap" ]
.RI [ \-\-ttl " seconds" ]
.br
.B shoal-token list
.br
.B shoal-token revoke
.I id
.SH DESCRIPTION
Creates, lists, and revokes credentials used to authenticate kernel clients.
The bearer secret produced by
.B create
is shown exactly once and is not recoverable through
.BR list .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI create " PRINCIPAL [PROFILE]"
Create a token for PRINCIPAL and an optional policy PROFILE.
.B \-\-cap CAP
is repeatable;
.B \-\-ttl SECONDS
sets an expiry duration.
.TP
.B list
Print token ID, principal, profile, and active or revoked state as tab-separated metadata.
.TP
.BI revoke " ID"
Mark ID revoked so it cannot authenticate a new session.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-cap " CAP"
Grant CAP to a newly created token; repeat for multiple capabilities.
.TP
.BI \-\-ttl " SECONDS"
Expire a new token after the specified duration.
.TP
.BR \-h , " \-\-help"
Print command help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V , " \-\-version"
Print the version and exit.
.SH OUTPUT
.B create
writes the bearer secret to standard output and the created token ID to standard error.
.B list
writes metadata only; revoke is silent on success.
.SH ERRORS
Unknown commands or options, missing values, invalid TTLs, unknown revoke IDs,
and token-store or encryption failures are reported without redisplaying existing secrets.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SHOAL_TOKEN_STORE
Override the token database path used by the kernel and token manager.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
shoal-token create automation restricted-agent --cap fs.read --ttl 3600
shoal-token list
shoal-token revoke TOKEN_ID
.EE
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on success and 1 for input, storage, encryption, or token lookup failures.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR shoal-mcp (1),
.BR shoal-kernel (1)
